From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:22:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/adbe: Switch the panel off in system sleep

In s2idle the iPad 5 panel stayed powered: the pipe kept scanning out the
black boot framebuffer to a panel whose TCON and source drivers ran on,
with only the backlight off. iOS turns the panel off on every display
sleep. AppleDPDisplayPowerController drops lcd_ldo, keeps it off at least
125 ms, and on enable waits for hot-plug detect (expected within 67 ms)
and lets the backlight on no earlier than 193 ms after the supply. The
DisplayPort driver, an Analogix DP core (AppleANXDPTX), then trains the
link again. Its event log on J71t shows a no-handshake (fast) training at
the link the boot loader set up: 4 lanes, 1.62 Gb/s, enhanced framing,
swing 0, pre-emphasis 0, ASSR on.

Do the same around system sleep, leaving the pipe and the transmitter as
the boot loader set them up; only the sink loses power:

- Before the first sleep, look up the supply and the backlight, and order
  sleep so that the pipe suspends before the PMU GPIO (behind I2C) and
  the backlight resumes after the pipe. Neither holds up probe.
- At suspend, after the CRTC is off and the pipe shows the black boot
  framebuffer, the supply goes off only if the live link passes every
  check the wake needs: AUX reads of the receiver capabilities and of the
  sink's link configuration, a lane status that reads trained, a sink
  that allows no-handshake training, a sink whose scrambler seed mode
  (ASSR) matches the transmitter's (0x614 bit 0), and a supply that reads
  on and then off. Otherwise the panel stays on for that sleep, with the
  reason logged. 50 ms after the supply goes off, the hot-plug detect
  level and one AUX read are logged as a witness that the sink went away.
- On resume, before the CRTC is restored: supply on after the 125 ms
  minimum (counted in boot time: s2idle stops the monotonic clock), wait
  for hot-plug detect, read the capabilities back over AUX, write the
  saved link configuration (D0, ASSR as the transmitter has it,
  downspread, rate, lane count), send TPS1 then TPS2 with the transmitter
  and the DPCD, then check the lane status. A failed wake retries the
  whole sequence twice. If the panel still does not come back, the
  backlight is held off, the supply is left on and panel-off sleeps stop.

AUX follows iOS's readDPCDGated/writeDPCDGated. Unlike the Analogix
layout, the request nibble sits next to address bits 19:16 at 0x7a0, the
length at 0x794, the data at 0xc00, and the buffer clears with 0x790 bit
9. Completion is DP_INT_STA bit 1, an error bit 0 with the cause in
AUX_CH_STA.

sleep_panel_off=0 keeps the panel on in sleep, as before. The debugfs
file adbe_panel runs the pre-sleep checks on demand, with AUX reads only,
so their result can be seen before any sleep.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c | 701 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 694 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
index c1af6ca06..aa9a2838b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
@@ -3,12 +3,14 @@
  * DRM/KMS driver for the Apple A9/A10 display pipe, disp0.
  *
  * iBoot leaves the eDP link, the panel and the timing generator running.
- * This driver adopts that mode and never programs timings, clocks or the
- * link. It offers one XRGB8888 primary plane. A new framebuffer reaches the
- * pipe through the ADP parameter FIFO, which holds the packet until the next
- * frame boundary and applies it there; the pipe then raises the "packet
- * applied" status bit, which completes the page flip. A flip event therefore
- * never arrives before the new buffer is being scanned out.
+ * This driver adopts that mode and never programs timings or clocks; it
+ * trains the link only after a sleep with the panel off (see below), with the
+ * boot loader's link settings. It offers one XRGB8888 primary plane. A new
+ * framebuffer reaches the pipe through the ADP parameter FIFO, which holds
+ * the packet until the next frame boundary and applies it there; the pipe
+ * then raises the "packet applied" status bit, which completes the page flip.
+ * A flip event therefore never arrives before the new buffer is being
+ * scanned out.
  *
  * The block is the ADBE back end of iOS's AppleH8ADBE0 kext
  * (AppleMobileADBE0, AppleH7DisplayPipe). Its FIFO port and layer registers
@@ -35,19 +37,33 @@
  * every buffer it handed to the pipe mapped until the pipe is seen reading a
  * newer one, and returns the DART to bypass, on the boot framebuffer, at
  * shutdown.
+ *
+ * In system sleep the panel supply goes off, as on iOS, where
+ * AppleDPDisplayPowerController switches the panel's lcd_ldo and the
+ * DisplayPort transmitter (an Analogix DP core) trains the link again on
+ * every wake. The pipe and the transmitter keep running as iBoot set them
+ * up: only the sink loses power. Before the supply is cut, the link must
+ * read back as trained over AUX and the supply must read on; otherwise the
+ * panel stays on for that sleep. On wake the link gets the boot loader's
+ * configuration and a no-handshake (fast) training, as iOS does, and the
+ * backlight comes on only after the link reads back trained.
  */
 
 #include <linux/aperture.h>
 #include <linux/apple-dart.h>
+#include <linux/backlight.h>
 #include <linux/console.h>
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/bits.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/driver.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_address.h>
@@ -59,13 +75,17 @@
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/scatterlist.h>
+#include <linux/seq_file.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/timer.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 #include <drm/clients/drm_client_setup.h>
+#include <drm/display/drm_dp.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
+#include <drm/drm_debugfs.h>
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_dumb_buffers.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fb_dma_helper.h>
@@ -149,6 +169,65 @@
 #define DART_PTE_VALID		BIT_ULL(0)
 #define DART_PTE_ADDR		GENMASK_ULL(35, 12)
 
+/*
+ * DisplayPort transmitter ("displayport,s8003", AppleANXDPTX), the "dp"
+ * window: an Analogix DP core, but AUX takes the request nibble next to
+ * address bits 19:16 and keeps its data at 0xc00, as iOS's readDPCDGated and
+ * writeDPCDGated use it. Status 0x3dc: bit 1 reply received, bit 0 AUX
+ * error (cause in 0x780[3:0]); iOS unmasks both in 0x3f8 for a transaction.
+ */
+#define DPTX_INT_STA		0x3dc
+#define DPTX_INT_STA_MASK	0x3f8
+#define DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR	BIT(0)
+#define DPTX_INT_RPLY		BIT(1)
+#define DPTX_SYS_CTL_3		0x608
+#define DPTX_SYS_CTL_3_HPD	BIT(6)
+#define DPTX_ASSR		0x614	/* bit 0: alternate scrambler seed (setASSREnabledGated) */
+#define DPTX_ASSR_EN		BIT(0)
+#define DPTX_TRAINING_PTN	0x688	/* [1:0] pattern, bit 5 scrambling off */
+#define DPTX_TRAINING_PTN_MASK	GENMASK(1, 0)
+#define DPTX_TRAINING_NO_SCRAMBLE BIT(5)
+#define DPTX_AUX_CH_STA		0x780
+#define DPTX_AUX_STATUS		GENMASK(3, 0)
+#define DPTX_AUX_STATUS_NACK	1
+#define DPTX_AUX_STATUS_TIMEOUT	2
+#define DPTX_AUX_STATUS_NACK_M	7
+#define DPTX_AUX_RX_COMM	0x78c
+#define DPTX_AUX_BUF_CTL	0x790
+#define DPTX_AUX_BUF_CLR	BIT(9)
+#define DPTX_AUX_BUF_COUNT	GENMASK(8, 0)
+#define DPTX_AUX_LEN		0x794	/* length - 1 */
+#define DPTX_AUX_ADDR_7_0	0x798
+#define DPTX_AUX_ADDR_15_8	0x79c
+#define DPTX_AUX_ADDR_19_16	0x7a0	/* [7:4] request, [3:0] address 19:16 */
+#define DPTX_AUX_CTL_2		0x7a4
+#define DPTX_AUX_EN		BIT(0)
+#define DPTX_AUX_ADDR_ONLY	BIT(1)
+#define DPTX_AUX_DATA(i)	(0xc00 + 4 * (i))
+#define DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_WRITE	0x80
+#define DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_READ	0x90
+#define DPTX_AUX_MAX		16
+#define DPTX_AUX_WAIT_US	20000
+#define DPTX_AUX_TRIES		5
+
+/*
+ * Panel power timing, AppleDPDisplayPowerController's defaults (no ADT
+ * override on J71t): the supply stays off at least 125 ms, hot-plug detect
+ * is expected 67 ms after it comes on, and the backlight waits 193 ms.
+ */
+#define ADBE_PANEL_OFF_MIN_MS	125
+#define ADBE_PANEL_HPD_MS	67
+#define ADBE_PANEL_BL_MS	193
+#define ADBE_PANEL_HPD_WAIT_US	(500 * USEC_PER_MSEC)
+#define ADBE_PANEL_AUX_WAIT_MS	500
+#define ADBE_PANEL_TRIES	3
+/* After the supply goes off: when to look whether the sink went away. */
+#define ADBE_PANEL_DROP_MS	50
+/* Fast training: each pattern for at least 500 us. */
+#define ADBE_TPS_US		1000
+/* DPCD 0x100..0x10a: the link the boot loader trained, replayed on wake. */
+#define ADBE_LINK_CFG_LEN	(DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET + 1)
+
 #define ADBE_ALIGN		64	/* plane base and stride */
 #define ADBE_ADDR_TAG		(ADBE_ALIGN - 1)	/* low bits of base/stride */
 #define ADBE_BUS_LIMIT		BIT_ULL(32)
@@ -172,6 +251,11 @@ static bool dart_scanout = true;
 module_param(dart_scanout, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dart_scanout,
 		 "Scan out through the display DART, so any dma-buf can be shown (reads back the active mode)");
+
+static bool sleep_panel_off = true;
+module_param(sleep_panel_off, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(sleep_panel_off,
+		 "Turn the panel supply off in system sleep and train the eDP link again on wake, as iOS (default 1)");
 #define ADBE_FLIP_VBLANKS	3	/* complete on VBI if bit 10 never comes */
 #define ADBE_FLIP_TIMEOUT_MS	100	/* complete anyway without an interrupt */
 #define ADBE_INTEN_VBLANK	(ADP_ST_VBI | ADP_ST_APPLIED)
@@ -228,6 +312,24 @@ struct adbe {
 	} hold[ADBE_HOLD_MAX];
 	unsigned int nhold;
 	struct delayed_work hold_work;
+
+	/*
+	 * Panel power over system sleep. The supply and the backlight are
+	 * looked up before the first sleep, not at probe, so that probe does
+	 * not wait for the PMU or the backlight.
+	 */
+	void __iomem *dp;
+	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
+	struct gpio_desc *lcd_ldo;
+	struct backlight_device *backlight;
+	struct device_link *ldo_link, *bl_link;
+	bool panel_ready;	/* supply and ordering in place */
+	bool panel_off;		/* the supply is off for this sleep */
+	bool panel_lost;	/* a wake did not bring the panel back */
+	bool bl_held;		/* backlight held off after a failed wake */
+	ktime_t panel_off_at;
+	u8 dpcd_caps[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE + 1];
+	u8 link_cfg[ADBE_LINK_CFG_LEN];
 };
 
 static struct adbe *to_adbe(struct drm_device *drm)
@@ -1792,6 +1894,552 @@ static int adbe_modeset_init(struct adbe *adbe)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* One native AUX transaction of 1..16 bytes, as AppleANXDPTXController. */
+static int adbe_aux_xfer(struct adbe *adbe, u32 request, u32 addr, u8 *buf,
+			 size_t len)
+{
+	void __iomem *dp = adbe->dp;
+	u32 ctl, mask, st, aux;
+	size_t i;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!len || len > DPTX_AUX_MAX)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	writel(len - 1, dp + DPTX_AUX_LEN);
+	writel(addr & 0xff, dp + DPTX_AUX_ADDR_7_0);
+	writel((addr >> 8) & 0xff, dp + DPTX_AUX_ADDR_15_8);
+	writel(request | ((addr >> 16) & 0xf), dp + DPTX_AUX_ADDR_19_16);
+	ctl = readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_CTL_2) & ~(DPTX_AUX_ADDR_ONLY | DPTX_AUX_EN);
+	writel(ctl, dp + DPTX_AUX_CTL_2);
+	writel(DPTX_AUX_BUF_CLR, dp + DPTX_AUX_BUF_CTL);
+	if (request == DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_WRITE)
+		for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
+			writel(buf[i], dp + DPTX_AUX_DATA(i));
+
+	writel(DPTX_INT_RPLY | DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR, dp + DPTX_INT_STA);
+	mask = readl(dp + DPTX_INT_STA_MASK);
+	writel(mask | DPTX_INT_RPLY | DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR, dp + DPTX_INT_STA_MASK);
+	writel(ctl | DPTX_AUX_EN, dp + DPTX_AUX_CTL_2);
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(dp + DPTX_INT_STA, st,
+				 st & (DPTX_INT_RPLY | DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR), 20,
+				 DPTX_AUX_WAIT_US);
+	writel(st & (DPTX_INT_RPLY | DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR), dp + DPTX_INT_STA);
+	writel(mask, dp + DPTX_INT_STA_MASK);
+
+	if (ret || (st & DPTX_INT_AUX_ERR)) {
+		/* iOS drops AUX_EN itself after a failed transaction. */
+		writel(readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_CTL_2) & ~DPTX_AUX_EN,
+		       dp + DPTX_AUX_CTL_2);
+		aux = readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_CH_STA) & DPTX_AUX_STATUS;
+		dev_dbg(adbe->drm.dev,
+			"AUX %s %#x: %s, AUX_CH_STA %#x AUX_RX_COMM %#x\n",
+			request == DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_READ ? "read" : "write", addr,
+			ret ? "no reply" : "error", aux,
+			readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_RX_COMM));
+		if (ret || aux == DPTX_AUX_STATUS_TIMEOUT)
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		if (aux == DPTX_AUX_STATUS_NACK || aux == DPTX_AUX_STATUS_NACK_M)
+			return -ENXIO;
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+
+	if (request == DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_READ) {
+		if (FIELD_GET(DPTX_AUX_BUF_COUNT,
+			      readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_BUF_CTL)) < len)
+			return -EPROTO;
+		for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
+			buf[i] = readl(dp + DPTX_AUX_DATA(i));
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Retried like commitAuxTransactionWithRetries; a NACK is final. */
+static int adbe_dpcd_xfer(struct adbe *adbe, u32 request, u32 addr, u8 *buf,
+			  size_t len)
+{
+	int ret = -EIO, tries;
+
+	for (tries = 0; tries < DPTX_AUX_TRIES; tries++) {
+		ret = adbe_aux_xfer(adbe, request, addr, buf, len);
+		if (!ret || ret == -ENXIO || ret == -EINVAL)
+			break;
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int adbe_dpcd_read(struct adbe *adbe, u32 addr, u8 *buf, size_t len)
+{
+	return adbe_dpcd_xfer(adbe, DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_READ, addr, buf, len);
+}
+
+static int adbe_dpcd_write(struct adbe *adbe, u32 addr, const u8 *buf,
+			   size_t len)
+{
+	return adbe_dpcd_xfer(adbe, DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_WRITE, addr, (u8 *)buf,
+			      len);
+}
+
+static int adbe_dpcd_writeb(struct adbe *adbe, u32 addr, u8 value)
+{
+	return adbe_dpcd_write(adbe, addr, &value, 1);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The transmitter's scrambler seed mode. The sink must match it: a mismatch
+ * still trains and locks, but every scrambled pixel is noise.
+ */
+static u8 adbe_source_assr(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	return readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_ASSR) & DPTX_ASSR_EN ?
+	       DP_ALTERNATE_SCRAMBLER_RESET_ENABLE : 0;
+}
+
+static unsigned int adbe_link_lanes(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	return adbe->link_cfg[DP_LANE_COUNT_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] &
+	       DP_LANE_COUNT_MASK;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The sink's view of the link: every lane has clock recovery, equalisation
+ * and symbol lock, and the lanes are aligned. Returns 0 or -EIO, and the
+ * status bytes 0x202..0x204 in @st.
+ */
+static int adbe_link_status(struct adbe *adbe, u8 st[3])
+{
+	unsigned int lane, lanes = adbe_link_lanes(adbe);
+	u8 want = DP_LANE_CR_DONE | DP_LANE_CHANNEL_EQ_DONE |
+		  DP_LANE_SYMBOL_LOCKED;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = adbe_dpcd_read(adbe, DP_LANE0_1_STATUS, st, 3);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	if (!lanes || lanes > 4)
+		return -EIO;
+	for (lane = 0; lane < lanes; lane++)
+		if (((st[lane / 2] >> (4 * (lane & 1))) & want) != want)
+			return -EIO;
+	if (!(st[2] & DP_INTERLANE_ALIGN_DONE))
+		return -EIO;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Train the link again with the configuration the boot loader left, as iOS
+ * does on every wake (its event log: TrainLink, 4 lanes, RBR, enhanced
+ * framing, Fast, no downspread, swing 0 / pre-emphasis 0; ASSR on). The
+ * sink advertises NO_AUX_HANDSHAKE_LINK_TRAINING, so the source sends TPS1
+ * then TPS2 for a fixed time and the sink locks without AUX handshakes.
+ * The transmitter's own link rate, lane count and drive levels are as the
+ * boot loader set them and are not touched.
+ */
+static int adbe_link_train(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	struct device *dev = adbe->drm.dev;
+	unsigned int lanes = adbe_link_lanes(adbe);
+	const u8 *cfg = adbe->link_cfg;
+	u8 tps[5] = { 0 }, st[3];
+	u32 ptn;
+	int ret;
+
+	ptn = readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN);
+	if (ptn & DPTX_TRAINING_PTN_MASK) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "transmitter left in training pattern %#x\n", ptn);
+		ptn &= ~(DPTX_TRAINING_PTN_MASK | DPTX_TRAINING_NO_SCRAMBLE);
+	}
+
+	ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_SET_POWER, DP_SET_POWER_D0);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_SET,
+				       (cfg[DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] &
+					~DP_ALTERNATE_SCRAMBLER_RESET_ENABLE) |
+				       adbe_source_assr(adbe));
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_DOWNSPREAD_CTRL,
+				       cfg[DP_DOWNSPREAD_CTRL - DP_LINK_BW_SET]);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_LINK_BW_SET, cfg[0]);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_LANE_COUNT_SET,
+				       cfg[DP_LANE_COUNT_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET]);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: link configuration write failed: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	writel(ptn | DPTX_TRAINING_NO_SCRAMBLE | DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_1,
+	       adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN);
+	tps[0] = DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_1 | DP_LINK_SCRAMBLING_DISABLE;
+	ret = adbe_dpcd_write(adbe, DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_SET, tps, 1 + lanes);
+	usleep_range(ADBE_TPS_US, 2 * ADBE_TPS_US);
+	if (!ret) {
+		writel(ptn | DPTX_TRAINING_NO_SCRAMBLE | DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_2,
+		       adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN);
+		tps[0] = DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_2 | DP_LINK_SCRAMBLING_DISABLE;
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_write(adbe, DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_SET, tps,
+				      1 + lanes);
+		usleep_range(ADBE_TPS_US, 2 * ADBE_TPS_US);
+	}
+	/* Back to the normal (scrambled) stream whatever happened. */
+	writel(ptn, adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_writeb(adbe, DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_SET,
+				       DP_TRAINING_PATTERN_DISABLE);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: training pattern write failed: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	ret = adbe_link_status(adbe, st);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: link not trained: lane status %3ph (%d)\n",
+			st, ret);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Look up the panel supply and the backlight once, before the first sleep,
+ * and order system sleep: the display pipe suspends before the PMU GPIO
+ * (behind I2C) and resumes after it, and the backlight resumes only after
+ * the pipe has brought the panel back.
+ */
+static void adbe_panel_attach(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	struct device *dev = adbe->drm.dev;
+	struct device_node *np;
+	struct gpio_desc *ldo;
+
+	if (adbe->panel_ready || !adbe->dp)
+		return;
+
+	if (!adbe->lcd_ldo) {
+		ldo = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "apple,lcd-ldo", GPIOD_ASIS);
+		if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(ldo)) {
+			if (PTR_ERR(ldo) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+				return;	/* the PMU is not there yet: next sleep */
+			dev_info(dev, "sleep: no panel supply (%pe), panel stays on\n",
+				 ldo);
+			adbe->dp = NULL;
+			return;
+		}
+		adbe->lcd_ldo = ldo;
+	}
+	if (!adbe->ldo_link) {
+		adbe->ldo_link = device_link_add(dev,
+			gpio_device_to_device(gpiod_to_gpio_device(adbe->lcd_ldo)),
+			DL_FLAG_STATELESS);
+		if (!adbe->ldo_link) {
+			dev_warn(dev, "sleep: cannot order against the panel supply\n");
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
+	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "backlight", 0);
+	if (np && !adbe->bl_link) {
+		adbe->backlight = of_find_backlight_by_node(np);
+		if (!adbe->backlight) {
+			of_node_put(np);
+			return;	/* not registered yet: next sleep */
+		}
+		adbe->bl_link = device_link_add(&adbe->backlight->dev, dev,
+						DL_FLAG_STATELESS);
+		if (!adbe->bl_link) {
+			dev_warn(dev, "sleep: cannot order the backlight after the panel\n");
+			put_device(&adbe->backlight->dev);
+			adbe->backlight = NULL;
+			of_node_put(np);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	of_node_put(np);
+	adbe->panel_ready = true;
+}
+
+static void adbe_panel_detach(void *data)
+{
+	struct adbe *adbe = data;
+
+	if (adbe->bl_link)
+		device_link_del(adbe->bl_link);
+	if (adbe->backlight)
+		put_device(&adbe->backlight->dev);
+	if (adbe->ldo_link)
+		device_link_del(adbe->ldo_link);
+}
+
+static int adbe_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action,
+			  void *data)
+{
+	struct adbe *adbe = container_of(nb, struct adbe, pm_nb);
+
+	if (action == PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE && sleep_panel_off)
+		adbe_panel_attach(adbe);
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
+static void adbe_pm_notify_remove(void *data)
+{
+	struct adbe *adbe = data;
+
+	unregister_pm_notifier(&adbe->pm_nb);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Before the supply goes off, everything the wake needs must already work
+ * on the live link: AUX, the sink's capabilities and its trained link
+ * configuration, the lane status check, and a supply that reads on. Any
+ * miss keeps the panel on for this sleep, as before.
+ */
+static const char *adbe_panel_gate(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	u8 caps[sizeof(adbe->dpcd_caps)], cfg[ADBE_LINK_CFG_LEN], st[3];
+	int ret;
+
+	if (adbe->panel_lost)
+		return "a wake did not bring it back earlier";
+	if (gpiod_get_direction(adbe->lcd_ldo) != GPIO_LINE_DIRECTION_OUT)
+		return "lcd_ldo is not an output";
+	if (gpiod_get_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo) != 1)
+		return "lcd_ldo does not read on";
+	if (readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN) & DPTX_TRAINING_PTN_MASK)
+		return "the transmitter is sending a training pattern";
+	if (adbe_dpcd_read(adbe, DP_DPCD_REV, caps, sizeof(caps)))
+		return "AUX read of the receiver capabilities failed";
+	if (!caps[DP_DPCD_REV] || !(caps[DP_MAX_LANE_COUNT] & DP_MAX_LANE_COUNT_MASK))
+		return "the receiver capabilities read back empty";
+	if (!(caps[DP_MAX_DOWNSPREAD] & DP_NO_AUX_HANDSHAKE_LINK_TRAINING))
+		return "the sink needs handshake link training";
+	if (adbe->dpcd_caps[DP_DPCD_REV] &&
+	    memcmp(caps, adbe->dpcd_caps, sizeof(caps)))
+		return "the receiver capabilities changed";
+	if (adbe_dpcd_read(adbe, DP_LINK_BW_SET, cfg, sizeof(cfg)))
+		return "AUX read of the link configuration failed";
+	if (!cfg[0] || !(cfg[DP_LANE_COUNT_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] & DP_LANE_COUNT_MASK) ||
+	    (cfg[DP_LANE_COUNT_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] & DP_LANE_COUNT_MASK) > 4)
+		return "the sink reports no trained link";
+	if ((cfg[DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] &
+	     DP_ALTERNATE_SCRAMBLER_RESET_ENABLE) != adbe_source_assr(adbe))
+		return "the transmitter and the sink disagree on ASSR";
+
+	memcpy(adbe->dpcd_caps, caps, sizeof(caps));
+	memcpy(adbe->link_cfg, cfg, sizeof(cfg));
+	ret = adbe_link_status(adbe, st);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_info(adbe->drm.dev, "sleep: live lane status %3ph (%d)\n",
+			 st, ret);
+		return "the live link does not read back as trained";
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The pre-sleep checks on demand, without a sleep: AUX reads only, nothing
+ * is written to the sink, the supply or the transmitter.
+ */
+static int adbe_panel_show(struct seq_file *m, void *data)
+{
+	struct drm_debugfs_entry *entry = m->private;
+	struct adbe *adbe = to_adbe(entry->dev);
+	const char *why;
+	u32 hpd;
+
+	seq_printf(m, "sleep_panel_off %d\n", sleep_panel_off);
+	if (adbe->dp)
+		adbe_panel_attach(adbe);
+	if (!adbe->dp) {
+		seq_puts(m, "no DisplayPort transmitter or panel supply: panel stays on in sleep\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+	hpd = readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_SYS_CTL_3);
+	seq_printf(m, "ready %d lost %d backlight %s held %d\n", adbe->panel_ready,
+		   adbe->panel_lost, adbe->backlight ? dev_name(&adbe->backlight->dev) : "none",
+		   adbe->bl_held);
+	seq_printf(m, "SYS_CTL_3 %#x (hpd %d) TRAINING_PTN %#x ASSR %#x\n", hpd,
+		   !!(hpd & DPTX_SYS_CTL_3_HPD),
+		   readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_TRAINING_PTN),
+		   readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_ASSR));
+	if (!adbe->lcd_ldo) {
+		seq_puts(m, "lcd_ldo not found yet\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+	seq_printf(m, "lcd_ldo direction %d value %d\n",
+		   gpiod_get_direction(adbe->lcd_ldo),
+		   gpiod_get_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo));
+	why = adbe_panel_gate(adbe);
+	seq_printf(m, "gate %s\n", why ? why : "pass: the supply would go off in sleep");
+	seq_printf(m, "dpcd 0x000 %*ph\n", (int)sizeof(adbe->dpcd_caps),
+		   adbe->dpcd_caps);
+	seq_printf(m, "dpcd 0x100 %*ph\n", (int)sizeof(adbe->link_cfg),
+		   adbe->link_cfg);
+	seq_printf(m, "ASSR transmitter %u sink %u\n", adbe_source_assr(adbe),
+		   adbe->link_cfg[DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_SET - DP_LINK_BW_SET] &
+		   DP_ALTERNATE_SCRAMBLER_RESET_ENABLE);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void adbe_panel_off(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	struct device *dev = adbe->drm.dev;
+	const char *why;
+	u8 dpcd_rev;
+	int rev;
+
+	if (!sleep_panel_off || !adbe->dp ||
+	    pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_ON)
+		return;
+	if (!adbe->panel_ready) {
+		dev_info(dev, "sleep: panel stays on: supply or backlight not found yet\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	why = adbe_panel_gate(adbe);
+	if (why) {
+		dev_info(dev, "sleep: panel stays on: %s\n", why);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo, 0);
+	if (gpiod_get_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo) != 0) {
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo, 1);
+		dev_info(dev, "sleep: panel stays on: lcd_ldo did not switch off\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	adbe->panel_off = true;
+	adbe->panel_off_at = ktime_get_boottime();
+
+	/*
+	 * Witness that the sink lost power: its hot-plug detect drops and AUX
+	 * gets no reply. Logged, not gated: the rail may decay slowly.
+	 */
+	msleep(ADBE_PANEL_DROP_MS);
+	rev = adbe_aux_xfer(adbe, DPTX_AUX_NATIVE_READ, DP_DPCD_REV, &dpcd_rev, 1);
+	dev_info(dev, "sleep: panel supply off (link %u lanes, bw %#x, ASSR %u); after %d ms: hpd %d, aux %d\n",
+		 adbe_link_lanes(adbe), adbe->link_cfg[0], adbe_source_assr(adbe),
+		 ADBE_PANEL_DROP_MS,
+		 !!(readl(adbe->dp + DPTX_SYS_CTL_3) & DPTX_SYS_CTL_3_HPD), rev);
+}
+
+/* Supply on, wait for the sink, train. Returns 0 once the link reads trained. */
+static int adbe_panel_power_up(struct adbe *adbe, ktime_t *on_at)
+{
+	struct device *dev = adbe->drm.dev;
+	u8 caps[sizeof(adbe->dpcd_caps)];
+	s64 off_ms;
+	ktime_t deadline;
+	u32 v;
+	int ret;
+
+	off_ms = ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get_boottime(), adbe->panel_off_at);
+	if (off_ms < ADBE_PANEL_OFF_MIN_MS)
+		msleep(ADBE_PANEL_OFF_MIN_MS - off_ms);
+
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo, 1);
+	*on_at = ktime_get();
+	if (gpiod_get_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo) != 1) {
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: lcd_ldo does not read on\n");
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+
+	msleep(ADBE_PANEL_HPD_MS);
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(adbe->dp + DPTX_SYS_CTL_3, v,
+				 v & DPTX_SYS_CTL_3_HPD, 1000,
+				 ADBE_PANEL_HPD_WAIT_US);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "eDP: no hot-plug detect (SYS_CTL_3 %#x), trying AUX\n",
+			 v);
+
+	/* The TCON answers AUX once it is up; iOS reads the caps first too. */
+	deadline = ktime_add_ms(ktime_get(), ADBE_PANEL_AUX_WAIT_MS);
+	do {
+		ret = adbe_dpcd_read(adbe, DP_DPCD_REV, caps, sizeof(caps));
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		msleep(10);
+	} while (ktime_before(ktime_get(), deadline));
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: sink does not answer AUX: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+	if (memcmp(caps, adbe->dpcd_caps, sizeof(caps))) {
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: receiver capabilities %*ph differ from before sleep\n",
+			(int)sizeof(caps), caps);
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+
+	ret = adbe_link_train(adbe);
+	if (ret)
+		ret = adbe_link_train(adbe);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Bring the panel back before the CRTC is restored: the pipe still shows the
+ * black boot framebuffer while the link trains. A failed attempt switches
+ * the supply off again and retries; after the last one the backlight is held
+ * off, so the panel is never lit without a trained link.
+ */
+static void adbe_panel_on(struct adbe *adbe)
+{
+	struct device *dev = adbe->drm.dev;
+	ktime_t start = ktime_get(), on_at = start;
+	s64 lit_ms;
+	int tries, ret = -EIO;
+
+	if (!adbe->panel_off && !adbe->panel_lost)
+		return;
+
+	for (tries = 0; tries < ADBE_PANEL_TRIES; tries++) {
+		if (tries || (!adbe->panel_off && adbe->panel_lost)) {
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo, 0);
+			adbe->panel_off_at = ktime_get_boottime();
+		}
+		ret = adbe_panel_power_up(adbe, &on_at);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		dev_warn(dev, "eDP: panel wake attempt %d failed: %d\n",
+			 tries + 1, ret);
+	}
+	adbe->panel_off = false;
+
+	if (ret) {
+		/* Leave the supply on: a later wake or a reboot may still recover. */
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(adbe->lcd_ldo, 1);
+		adbe->panel_lost = true;
+		if (adbe->backlight && !adbe->bl_held) {
+			backlight_disable(adbe->backlight);
+			adbe->bl_held = true;
+		}
+		dev_err(dev, "eDP: panel did not come back after %d attempts: backlight held off, panel-off sleeps stopped\n",
+			ADBE_PANEL_TRIES);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* iOS lets the backlight on no earlier than 193 ms after the supply. */
+	lit_ms = ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), on_at);
+	if (lit_ms < ADBE_PANEL_BL_MS)
+		msleep(ADBE_PANEL_BL_MS - lit_ms);
+	if (adbe->bl_held) {
+		backlight_enable(adbe->backlight);
+		adbe->bl_held = false;
+	}
+	if (adbe->panel_lost)
+		dev_info(dev, "eDP: panel recovered\n");
+	adbe->panel_lost = false;
+	dev_info(dev, "wake: panel back, link %u lanes trained in %lld ms\n",
+		 adbe_link_lanes(adbe), ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start));
+}
+
 /*
  * Powering disp0 or dp off resets the pipe and the eDP link, which this
  * driver cannot bring back. Hold every listed domain while bound.
@@ -1838,6 +2486,16 @@ static int adbe_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(adbe->regs))
 		return PTR_ERR(adbe->regs);
 
+	/* The DisplayPort transmitter: only system sleep uses it (panel power). */
+	if (platform_get_resource_byname(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, "dp")) {
+		adbe->dp = devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(pdev, "dp");
+		if (IS_ERR(adbe->dp)) {
+			dev_warn(dev, "no DisplayPort transmitter window (%pe): panel stays on in sleep\n",
+				 adbe->dp);
+			adbe->dp = NULL;
+		}
+	}
+
